<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter of Cantabria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Peter, Duke of Cantabria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabria">Cantabria</a> was a duke of Cantabria in the early 8th century, known only from the Asturian chronicles of the late 9th century, which claim he descended from the Visigothic kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liuvigild">Leovigild</a> and Reccared. His son Alfonso married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ermesinda">Ermesinda</a>, daughter of Pelagius, and became King Alfonso I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> in 739, uniting Cantabria with the Asturian kingdom.</p></div>
